summary:
  "virgin radio uk" is read as two tags inside Britain instead of a name.

history:
  The facet reading accepts unknown words beside a country, which is what
  makes "synthwave uk" work. Words that belong to station names are the
  fence: one of them and the query goes to the name roads untouched.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SearchLogic.js

find:
                  if (NAME_WORDS.hasOwnProperty(w) || /[0-9]/.test(w)) return null;

replace:
                  if (/[0-9]/.test(w)) return null;

expect:
  Killed by tst_searchlogic::test_station_names_are_left_to_the_name_roads.
  Line-neutral.
